  "solution": {
    "text": "In ZnS structure, sulphides occupy all the lattice points while Zn<sup>2</sup><sup>+</sup> ions are present in alternative tetrahedral voids.<br /><math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi></math> has FCC structure and <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math> atom occupied all octahedral hole.<br /><math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> has FCC structure and all T-holes will occupied by guest.<br /><math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math> has FCC sturcture and all T-holes will occupied by guest."
